        Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Step 15 \[LongDash] Simplify the \
relative-demand relation. The next cell performs several algebraic operations \
in one block. (1) $Assumptions records positive quantities and prices, \
0<\[Omega]<1, \[Sigma]>0 and \[Sigma]\[NotEqual]1. (2) Together collects \
fractions. (3) Numerator extracts the numerator of the left-hand expression, \
and Cancel removes common factors. A denominator may be discarded only when \
it is nonzero on the admissible domain. (4) FactorList separates factors; the \
fixed selection fac[[3,1]] assumes a particular factor ordering and is \
therefore fragile. (5) The substitution x=Cne[t]^(1/\[Sigma]) makes the \
selected relation linear in x. Solve obtains its value. (6) Raising the \
positive solution to \[Sigma] returns to Cne[t]. PowerExpand can ignore \
branch restrictions, so its output should be checked against the original \
positive-domain condition. The expected real-valued result is \
Cne[t]=Eh[t]((1\[Minus]\[Omega])pe[t]/\[Omega])^\[Sigma]. In particular, \
products of separately written negative-base fractional powers in the saved \
output should be recombined through the positive ratio before any numerical \
interpretation.", "Text"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
